Hi,

First, I'm not sure where this message should be going, so perhaps you 
can forward it to the appropriate place.

Anyway, I just wanted to write a quick thank-you note to the developers 
of ALSA, I'm still fairly new to Linux and by no means an audio 
professional, but I just switched from default OSS/Free sound drivers to 
ALSA, and I have to say it's made a world of difference in audio quality 
from my computer. I've got fairly good speakers hooked up and had become 
fairly acclimatised to ordinary sound quality, didn't even think there 
was anything "wrong." But ALSA made such a drastic difference, I'm now 
amazed by every sound that comes out of the computer and going through 
hundreds of songs I've listened to many times before, just to hear the 
"new and improved" versions. Thanks very much for making it possible, 
and even relatively easy for a new user such as myself to figure out and 
install.

If you're interested, the reason I bothered to switch in the first place 
is that I was interested in trying some Hard Drive multitrack recorders 
under Linux, and Ardour, seemingly the most sophisticated, requires ALSA 
(as you likely already knew). Anyway, one small bit of serendipity, and 
the whole computer audio experience has been much improved.


Thanks again, and good luck with ongoing development,

Daniel Holt
d_holt@canada.com



